BT /F1 10 Tf 50 720 Td (IN THE SUPREME COURT OF INDIA
AT NEW DELHI

CASE NO: W.P.\(Crl.\) No. 89 of 2026
CNR NUMBER: SCIN010034562026
DECISION DATE: 2026-01-22
YEAR: 2026

CORAM / BENCH:
Hon'ble Constitution Bench \(5 Judges\)

PARTIES:
Association for Democratic Reforms \(ADR\)
... Appellant\(s\) / Petitioner\(s\)
Versus
Union of India & Election Commission of India
... Respondent\(s\) / State

STATUTORY PROVISIONS & ACTS REFERRED:
Representation of the People Act 1951, Constitution of India

SECTIONS & CLAUSES UNDER CONSIDERATION:
RPA Section 33A, Article 19\(1\)\(a\), Article 324

KEY LEGAL DOMAINS & TOPICS:
Electoral Reforms, Voter Right to Information, Asset Disclosure, Article 19\(1\)\(a\), Free and Fair Elections

================================================================================
                                   JUDGMENT
================================================================================

1. FACTUAL MATRIX:
Petition seeking direction to ECI to mandate disclosure of virtual digital assets \(cryptocurrency, NFTs\) and offshore trust holdings by contesting candidates.

2. ISSUES FRAMED FOR ADJUDICATION:
1. Does voter right to information under Article 19\(1\)\(a\) encompass disclosure of digital and offshore assets of candidates?

3. STATUTORY FRAMEWORK & PRECEDENTS:
Voters' right to know candidate credentials flows from freedom of speech and expression under Article 19\(1\)\(a\) as held in Union of India v. ADR \(2002\).

4. RATIO DECIDENDI:
Right to informed choice is an integral facet of Article 19\(1\)\(a\); candidates must disclose all digital assets, cryptocurrencies, and offshore holdings in Form 26 affidavits.

5. FINAL DISPOSITION & ORDER:
Writ Petition Allowed; Mandatory disclosure of candidate digital assets and offshore interests directed.

Decreed and ordered accordingly.

Hon'ble Constitution Bench \(5 Judges\)
Supreme Court of India
[LEXGUARD CRYPTOGRAPHIC VERIFIED REPOSITORY RECORD]
